From e20f57c53164e1e9ad093351930436ea3814681b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 18:52:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] world-data: mod values kept in the world (FORK-36, API 47)

world-data.get/set/remove/keys keep byte values under <mod id>:<path> keys,
up to 256 KiB each and 64 per mod, saved with the world in
data/horizon/mod_world_data.bin (Mekanism's SavedData: frequencies, owners,
security). Part of capability world. Harness: world-data step and check,
kept across a reload; example world-data-probe.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RYe92n7spgy8vtm4CovRWA
